Quick answer (general rule)
- For most countries and for airlines, your passport should be valid for at least six months beyond your intended stay or beyond the end date of your visa. If your passport expires less than six months after your planned exit/visa end date, that's likely "too close" and you should renew before travel or before submitting the visa application.

Why this matters
- Border control or the airline may deny boarding/entry if your passport validity is too short.
- Visa-issuing embassies/consulates usually enforce their own validity requirements when they process applications.

