- Which country’s visa are you applying for?
- Which expiry date are you referring to (passport, green card, driver’s license)?
- What is the passport expiry date and the visa start/end or planned travel dates? (You do not need to provide your SSN—just dates.)

Next steps you can take right away
- Check the embassy/consulate website for that country’s passport-validity rule (many list “6 months beyond intended stay” explicitly).
- If your passport doesn’t meet the requirement, renew it before applying or travel. Look into expedited renewal options if time is tight.
- Contact the consulate or the airline if you’re unsure—they can confirm what they require.

If you tell me the passport expiry date and the visa or travel dates (no SSN), I’ll calculate whether you meet the 6-month rule and suggest next steps.

