- If you plan to enter on July 1, 2026 and your visa covers 6 months, your planned departure ≈ Jan 1, 2027.
- Add 6 months buffer → required passport validity >= July 1, 2027.
- If your passport expires before July 1, 2027, renew it before applying.

4) Caveats:
- Some countries require only 3 months beyond departure (e.g., some Schengen rules) or have different rules for visas vs. entry. Always confirm with the destination country’s consulate/immigration website.
- If you’re applying for the visa months before travel, check whether the consulate measures the 6‑month requirement from visa issue date, entry date, or planned departure — rules vary.

