Quick answer first: an SSN does not expire, so the number itself isn't the issue for a visa. What matters is the expiry date of the travel document (usually your passport) or any ID the visa application asks about.

A few points and next steps:
- If you actually meant passport expiry: many countries require your passport to be valid for at least six months beyond your intended date of entry or beyond the date you leave. Other countries require only that the passport be valid for the duration of stay or three months beyond departure. It varies by destination and visa type.
- If you meant some other document (driver’s license, national ID), check the specific visa/embassy requirements — they’ll list required document validity.
- What I need from you to give a specific answer: the destination country (or consulate) and the passport expiry date (or your planned travel dates). With that I can tell you whether the expiry is too close.
- Security note: you included a full SSN in the message. Please avoid posting full SSNs or other sensitive PII here. If you only need to reference it, give just the last four digits (which you already provided). I will not send or store that full SSN for you.

If you tell me the country and the passport expiry (or travel dates), I’ll check the typical requirement and tell you whether you should renew before applying.

